  "facts": {
    "district": [
      "native GetCurrentDistrictV9 authorizes one-shot fresh fix, stops it, then checks independent GeoConvert availability before parcel request",
      "actual GeoConvert uses configured bundle/ability via ConnectAbility, actual IRemoteObject request/results; no provider geocoding database/algorithm is supplied by that framework",
      "RO07 exact four-pattern actual source inventory finds geocoder parameter names only at declaration; not an exhaustive semantic search",
      "fixed official base_location code-map says offline conversion depends on product/provider and entry points do not imply it",
      "fixed SIG Flutter geocoding full OHOS code/module is an HAR public API consumer, not a GeoConvert remote ability",
      "RO06 actual native call order is StartDistrictLocating -> wait location -> StopLocating -> fresh-location validation -> GeoConvert availability -> 801; a stub/module 801 before a real fix must fail the source-bound native interval oracle."
    ],
    "BLE": [
      "complete current OHOS BLE callback/filter/ownership/stop framework exists",
      "current HCI loads libbt_vendor.z.so / BLUETOOTH_VENDOR_LIB_INTERFACE and uses vendor-supplied H4/MCT FDs; kernel BT_LE setting does not determine userspace HCI support",
      "BCM board complete vendor implementation opens userial and runs board firmware initialization; GN selects BCM4362A2.hcd",
      "Unisoc implementation is integrated-7885 vendor HAL and hardware-specific encrypted prebuilt",
      "manifest-listed fixed SIG Cordova complete tree has Android/iOS/macOS/Windows clients, no OHOS HCI controller adapter",
      "RO08 complete current device/qemu source plus full actual git tree exposes no vendor HCI/controller target or artifact; the only source Bluetooth names outside kernel configs are unused ALSA card constants. The exact searched terms and this repository/product boundary do not prove absence in all repositories.",
      "RO08 complete BCM userial/upio/hardware sources show rk3568 /dev/ttyS8, dayu210 /dev/ttyS9, rfkill power, actual HCI_RESET/BCM firmware command exchange and vendor-specific .hcd; changing a device path does not provide a controller.",
      "RO06 actual getState NAPI/client/stub/server path requires no Bluetooth permission; it can return OFF when the remote proxy is absent, so OFF is diagnostic only."
    ]
  },
